    "q-112406": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112406",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Let $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where ${b}_{1}={c}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2}=-{c}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} \\\\  & =2{c}_{2}-{c}_{1} \\\\  & =2{c}_{2}+(-{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
