    "q-35258": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35258",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=5{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=4{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3{b}_{1}-7{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-7{b}_{2}+3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}(5{b}_{2})+\\frac{3}{4}(4{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}{c}_{1}+\\frac{3}{4}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-35258-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]",
