    "q-81227": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81227",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=-{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=2{b}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2}+7{b}_{3} \\\\  & =7{b}_{3}+4{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-7(-{b}_{3})+8(\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{1})-(2{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =-7{c}_{1}+8{c}_{2}-{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-81227-a",
