    "q-112656": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112656",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=4{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=2{b}_{1}$ and ${c}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2}+8{b}_{3} \\\\  & =8{b}_{3}+2{b}_{1}+2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =2(4{b}_{3})+2{b}_{1}+2\\cdot 2(\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+4{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
