    "q-113095": {
      "dom_id": "step-q113095",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=-{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. Adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}={b}_{1}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}={c}_{1}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=2({c}_{1}+{c}_{2})-{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}={c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2} \\\\  & =4({c}_{1}+{c}_{2})-2({c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}-2{c}_{1}-4{c}_{2} \\\\  & =2{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
