    "q-81230": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81230",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}={b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. By adding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=2{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}={b}_{1}+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =7{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\  & =7(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2})+(\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{c}_{1}-\\frac{7}{2}{c}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{c}_{2} \\\\  & =4{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-81230-a",
