    "q-80830": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80830",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}},$ where ${c}_{1}=-{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are given that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=-{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}={b}_{2}-{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=-{c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{2}=-{c}_{1}-{b}_{1}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{1}=-{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3{b}_{1}+5{b}_{2} \\\\  & =3(-{c}_{1}-{c}_{2})+5(-{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-3{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}-5{c}_{1} \\\\  & =-8{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
